# Line endings: the bash scripts must stay LF. Under CRLF (Git for Windows
# autocrlf), bash dies on '\r': command not found. The release repo carries this
# rule at its root, but a copied core with a fresh `git init` would lose it —
# so the core ships its own.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The journal, when several people share this core (0.14): each one prepends
# entries under the H1 of log.md, so two clones that both wrote since the last
# pull would conflict on every merge. The built-in union driver keeps both
# sides' added lines, with no conflict marker: exactly the semantics of a
# journal you only add to. Only the two journals, anchored: a knowledge page
# is rewritten in place, and union there would keep both versions side by
# side, a silent duplicate. The same holds inside the journal for any line
# edited rather than prepended: with several people, its frontmatter timestamp
# is never bumped, and a rotation waits until everyone has pushed (Spec §4).
/log.md merge=union
/knowledge-base/log.md merge=union
